          "title": "Warp &amp; Weft: Threads of Our Doctoral Journeys",
          "text": "<p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Doctoral research can be a lonely process. The puzzlement and uncertainty that accompany our solo decisions destabilize us from time to time. Ultimately, this makes us more confident and knowledgeable researchers, but not without stress.</p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><br></p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">During the pandemic, students at The Ohio State University created a research collective, trace/layer/play, to support one another. The collective fostered more than motivation and encouragement; it incited new ways to incubate ideas as their research unfolded. Inspired by trace/layer/play, we formed our own collective, Warp &amp; Weft. The collective provides structure across our disciplines (art education, museum curation and education, libraries, and archives) to help each of us make our dissertations a little less lonely for each other.</p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><br></p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Take a few steps with us on our PhD journeys. Each section will highlight our research topic during one stage of the messy process of academic thinking. We invite you to add your own ideas and perspectives to the interactive elements.</p>"
