          "text": "<p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Early in my doctoral journey, I thought of research like a puzzle. Only, it's a puzzle where you have no idea what the final image looks like, you get to pick the pieces, and if you have a piece that doesn't quite fit but you like it, then you just kind of jam it in there and then make it work somehow....</p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><br></p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The puzzle metaphor fell apart pretty quickly.</p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><br></p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font: 400 12px Helvetica; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">So, instead, let's think of research as a Jenga tower. The blocks might represent the literature you've reviewed, the data you've collected, or even the playlist you put on while you work. Find a blank block and make it your own, try building something with the blocks, or try to add to someone else's creation.</p>"
