      "infoHotspots": [
        {
          "yaw": -2.28318331808466,
          "pitch": -0.05833753830329336,
          "title": "Cat: Disseminating Research and Narratives",
          "text": "<div>Experiences give way to opportunity.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Opportunity to understand.&nbsp;</div><div>Opportunity to recognize oneself in another individual’s journey.&nbsp;</div><div>Opportunity to see another individual’s point of view.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>When first starting out in the doctoral journey, I knew that the way I wanted to share the data and the experiences would not be wholly “traditional”. I have pushed back on “traditional” in academia, acknowledging that writing is not my biggest strength. I believe that the visual can be as valuable or more valuable in communicating experiences as the written word.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>This collection of panels is presented chronologically as they appear through the dissertation. The panels are pieces of the research and illustrations of the experiences shared through the interviews. They are presented here as if quilted together by the threads of the research, allowing you, the viewer, to explore the research and experiences of itinerancy in art education.</div>"
        },
        {
          "yaw": -2.221760498326324,
          "pitch": 0.1494244939427709,
          "title": "Sharing Experiences through Visual Narratives",
          "text": "<div>I invite you to share an experience in this visual format. Is it related to your teaching experience, time in a classroom, experience as a student?&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Experiences and understanding or identifying similarities aid in our social constructs. (I don’t like this yet)&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Share (and these can remain anonymous or you can use a pseudonym):&nbsp;</div><div>A teaching experience.&nbsp;</div><div>An experience as a student here on the campus.&nbsp;</div><div>An experience that shaped who you are.&nbsp;</div><div>An important aspect of who you are.&nbsp;</div><div>An experience from when you were an art student in school.</div>"
        }
      ]
